      "reasons": [
        "The source supports that convolutional kernels are used in deep learning for genome prediction and can be arranged sequentially or in a parallel structure, but it does not define convolution as a general learning concept or state that its purpose is to capture complex, often nonlinear patterns.",
        "The phrase “either in sequence or in parallel structures” is only partially supported: the packet mentions sequential convolutional kernels and a parallel convolutional attention network, but not a general either/or definition of convolutional kernels.",
